+    /* NEUTRON: a viewport change (crop/size) is CLIENT-surface state and shows only when that surface commits; the
+     * position is parent state and shows with the commit below. Left to the app's next present, a container
+     * scrolling a video moved it at once but cropped it a frame late (flicker at the clip edge), and a paused
+     * video kept a stale crop for good (scrolled back into view, it stayed 1x1 = gone). Lightroom Classic's
+     * What's New, 2026-10-13. So when nothing is presenting to it (present_busy, gdi_driver.h; Vulkan only --
+     * buffer_width is set by its present path), commit it HERE, synchronized, so crop and position land in the
+     * same parent commit. If a present is in flight, it carries the change (or wayland_client_surface_present
+     * commits it right after). */
